# Documentation authority metadata schema (DOC-META-001)

## Purpose

PSR-2a establishes the **machine-readable contract** for active documentation.
[`docs/index.yaml`](../index.yaml) is the sole registry of active docs. Historical
phase packs remain on disk until PSR-2c archive moves; they are **not** active
authority unless listed in the index with `status: active`.

## Required frontmatter fields (active docs)

| Field | Type | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | string | Stable doc id (`PSR-001`, `DOC-META-001`, `DG-REM-001`, …) |
| `role` | enum | Exactly one of the roles below |
| `owner` | string | Team/role accountable for correctness |
| `status` | enum | `active` \| `draft` \| `deprecated` \| `archived` |
| `last_verified` | date | ISO date `YYYY-MM-DD` of last human/machine verification |
| `verified_sha` | string | Full or short git SHA when content was verified |
| `supersedes` | string[] | Doc ids or paths this replaces (may be empty) |
| `superseded_by` | string \| null | Successor id/path when deprecated/archived |
| `evidence` | string[] | Paths to proofs, snapshots, or related evidence (may be empty) |

Optional but recommended: `title`, `format`, `program_id`, `wave`.

### Compatibility

Legacy `doc_role` may remain during transition. When both are present, **`role`
wins**. New docs must not invent `doc_role` values outside the role map below.

## Allowed `role` values

| role | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `canonical` | Current source of truth for a concern (architecture, remediation program) |
| `standard` | Normative contract / schema / platform standard |
| `adr` | Architecture decision record |
| `runbook` | Operational procedure |
| `audit_snapshot` | Immutable dated audit / inventory / train ledger |
| `evidence` | Supporting proof, example, classification pack (not sole authority) |
| `archive` | Explicitly historical; not active authority |

## `docs/index.yaml` shape

```yaml
schema_version: 1
program_id: PSR-001
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
verified_sha: <sha>
roles: [canonical, standard, adr, runbook, audit_snapshot, evidence, archive]
documents:
  - id: DOC-META-001
    path: docs/standards/doc-authority-metadata.schema.mdoc
    role: standard
    owner: platform-architecture
    status: active
    last_verified: YYYY-MM-DD
    verified_sha: <sha>
    supersedes: []
    superseded_by: null
    evidence: []
```

Rules:

1. Every `status: active` document used as authority **must** appear in
   `documents`.
2. Paths are repo-relative and must exist.
3. `id` values are unique within the index.
4. Index `role`/`status` must match file frontmatter for seeded docs.
5. Absence from the index does **not** delete a file; it means the file is not
   yet claimed as active authority (PSR-2c will archive closed packs).

## Validation

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-2a-validate-docs-index.mjs
```

Ops-only (not a new public root command). Exit `0` on pass; non-zero lists
violations. Full `guard:docs-manifest` / `guard:doc-frontmatter` land when PSR-2
contracts the active set further and can replace or join an existing guard
family (PSR-3 rule: no net-new root command without merge).

## Out of scope for PSR-2a

- TEMP promotion / zero tracked→ignored refs (PSR-2b)
- Phase pack moves to `docs/archive/` (PSR-2c)
- ROOT_COMMAND_* consolidation to ≤3 artifacts (PSR-2c)
- Committing the eight deferred dirty docs from PSR-0b without classification
